node_modules/
android/
ios/*
www/

# ios/ is otherwise fully ignored (regenerated by `npx cap sync`, so not
# meant to be tracked wholesale) — but hand-edited native config like
# Info.plist has repeatedly gotten wiped out by exactly that regeneration,
# costing a lot of re-diagnosis each time (missing camera/location
# permission strings, URL schemes, UIMainStoryboardFile, ...). Tracking
# just this file gives it a real backup/history instead of only ever
# existing on one Mac's disk.
#
# `ios/` alone (no wildcard) prunes the whole directory during traversal,
# and no amount of `!` negation further down ever reopens it — git simply
# never looks inside. `ios/*` instead excludes everything ios/ currently
# contains one level at a time, which negation patterns *can* still see
# and override. Every intermediate directory on the path to the one file
# that actually matters here needs its own `!.../` + `!.../*` pair, or the
# same pruning problem just recurs one level down.
!ios/App/
!ios/App/*
!ios/App/App/
!ios/App/App/Info.plist
